{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton","id":1555369,"title":"Great Leap Outwards Quesiton","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-11T12:27:14-08:00","id":1555369,"title":"Great Leap Outwards Quesiton","content":"I was thinking about the whole situation and how plausible that sounded.<br /> Similarly I have heard arguments for either side, Kuei Jin and Kindred.<br /> <br /> I think socially Kindred possess more advantages with Presence, Dominate and Blood Bonds. They also have more resources at home front and in easier time feeding. Their more combat oriented disciplines are often more straightforward to use at the very least.<br /> Where Kuei Jin seem to dominate is seem to be magic and everything related. Like access to Umbra, diplomacy with supernatural creatures, etc. Also they can make Devil Children, dhampirs and Bakemono in quite some numbers. While these are better then Ghouls, they also attract more attention - first of all from werewolves and Pentex. Where they will not have much diplomatic pull.<br /> <br /> For ease sake let us assume a simple situation. A single Wu vs similar number of kindred. Let's say anarch Brujah with 2 in every clan discipline, 3 in combat abilities/traits, WP5-6 and armed with desert eagles and bowie knives. I think this is a reasonable straightforward estimate without getting too complicated.<br /> <br /> On the other side we have a Wu that had been mostly quickly thrown together, so nothing and no one important is lost if they die. I say, let's keep physical and combat stats the same, But add 1 more WP. Disciplines 3 or 4, because they are harder to learn. as they are aimed at combat, I think they would be taught combat Disciplines. I think something like Demon Shintai 2 (+dex,+str, any 2 mutaions), Yang Chi 1 and Ghost-flame 1 seem reasonable? In addition, they may throw XP together to get a Nushi/Totem. This is where it gets very interesting. Yuki allows to stake vampires with melee weapons at +2 dice, Crab or Shuang allow to step sideways with ease, while Byakko and the Archer give aggravated attacks. for more info see <a href=\"https://kosaten2003.tripod.com/nushi.html\" target=\"_blank\">HERE</a>.<br /> <br /> Besides that Kuei Jin all have death/life sight, can manifest demonic maw for 2 demon chi and deal +2 aggravated damage with it if I remember correctly. lvl1 ghost-flame also stacks with demon maw, so it would be something like +3 aggregated damage with fire qualities. Vampires can buff physical characteristics with blood, while Kuei Jin can buff it depending on disciplines they have (stamina and strength with listed, if I remember correctly?)<br /> <br /> While magical weaponry is available for Kuei Jin, I am not sure it would be spent on frontline fighters in that conflict. Magical items are still valuable. But, I think they could be given Awakened items. Sure it is annoying for the sorcerer to be casting that rite time after time, but they need no great investment. So something like unnaturally sharp blades, or guns that never miss.<br /> <br /> Do you think this is reasonable? and how do you think the fight would go? Let's keep it relatively simple and street level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T14:24:42-08:00","id":1555373,"title":"","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> This is all very interesting stuff and talks a great deal about the differences between the Kuei Jin and Kindred's power sets but I think it kind of ignores the two larger issues of whatever will happen with the Great Leap Outward (what a terrible name) and any war between the Wan Kuei and the Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>1. What is the actual goal of the Great Leap Outward?</b><br /> <br /> There's a not unconvincing argument that the Great Leap Outward is a scam. One thing that is notable in the modern era that was true in previous ones is the fact that the Elders of the Wan Kuei are no more actually concerned about their younger members than the Western Kindred. Many more modern Wan Kuei are being born that have very little of the spiritual devotions or cultural history that the ancients do but are still born because Hell spits them out.<br /> This &quot;conspiracy theory&quot; is that the Great Leap Outward was nothing more than an attempt to thin the ranks of the young by sending them on an in-universe racist war that got them out of Asia and used them as cannon fodder against (as Hamlet would say), a foreign quarrel. They're not meant to actually win any war here but die.<br /> <br /> <b>2. The logistics of the Great Leap Outward favor the Western Kindred</b><br /> <br /> Part of this is due to the fact that I'm not 100% sure that Western Wan Kuei even exist. Whatever it is about the dragon nests or the Underworld in the area around China, Japan, India, and so on is not necessarily the case in America. Have there ever been any Kindred of the East born in California? I'm not sure. However, the simple fact is that taking the territory of the Western Kindred doesn't really do the Wan Kuei any favors. They can't make other Wan Kuei and Western Kindred don't have dragon nodes: that's something that is reserved for mages and werewolves.<br /> Every Western Kindred can make more of their kind and refill their power by draining the nearest mortal. The Wan Kuei? Well, they would have to expand their war against California shapeshifters and sorcerers.<br /> <br /> <b>3. The two major powers don't actually care</b><br /> <br /> As with many wars throughout history, the people least important to the war are those fighting it. The younger Wan Kuei and Anarchs doing battle for the state of California have more in common with each other than they do their respective Elders. They're only being pushed into the actual battle for dominion by outside forces who wish the other would wipe them other. It NIGHTS OF PROPECHY, the Kindred of the Camarilla actually just decide to pay the Wan Kuei off and the latter are willing to do it. The Camarilla would love to have Los Angeles back but the Wan Kuei thinning the herd of the Anarchs is fine by them as well. Vannevar Thomas might want San Fransisco back but the police state as described in San Fransisco by Night is an untenable one to begin with. It's one run by racist Wan Kuei who don't realize they're incredibly expendable.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Bloodlines may actually be the ending of the Great Leap Outward</b><br /> <br /> Say what you will about Ming Xiao but she was an actual Elder of the Wan Kuei and the head of the Los Angeles portion of the group. The Fledgling destroys her and a huge number of her military forces as well as the experiments they were running on Western Kindred. It certainly eradicates their forces there. Depending on how you view the importance of the war, it may actually have crippled the Kuei Jin's ability to fight in California.\u200b Among the Kuei Jin, the numbers wiped out by the Fledgling are not replaceable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T16:32:03-08:00","id":1555378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton#post1555369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about the whole situation and how plausible that sounded.<br /> Similarly I have heard arguments for either side, Kuei Jin and Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the whole exercise is skewed and oversimplified.<br /> <br /> Comparing builds like that is only relevant if you stipulate a very narrow question and strict conditions for making them, like comparing two starting characters by the rules for a death battle at a white room scenario without hiding places. That's fun, but says absolutely nothing about how they compare as warring factions in a particular area.<br /> <br /> First things first, neither build is really likely. Starting characters by the rules are PCs, they're young, but above average, not representatives of what an average character of that age will be like. Or any age, because on top of that characters within the story are unlikely to follow any &quot;combo&quot;, as they don't develop their stats to fill a PC role, they just live their lives. So characters on each side will vary greatly and very few, even if selected as warriors, will be anything like a combat-oriented PC.<br /> <br /> Second, it depends far more on their respective resources as factions than their individual powers. The struggle is not a sequence of direct skirmishes between individuals until one side is wiped, it is a complex mix of plots, political maneuvers, disputes for influence and money and much more. Even actual killings are more probably through traps, ambushes and other underhanded tactics than thugs in the streets hitting each other.<br /> <br /> Being able to achieve your goals without a fight is generally the best option in any conflict, and doubly so in the WoD, and being caught usually means retreating is more important than engaging interlopers, because your plans are probably already compromised. Actual fights are either for very specific strategic goals, result of massive failures, or completely unimportant. If winning a fight is actually relevant, each one will try to stack the chances in their favor as much as possible, so it won't be one-on-one. Fair fights are for sports and movies.<br /> <br /> Even if you ignore <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>' points (and I think they're fair even if not necessarily the original intent of the authors), conflicts of this scale are not just a series of PC fights\u200b. PCs get away doing things directly because they're the protagonists of a story, their actions are aggrandized by design, but the bulk of the conflict isn't like that. And I agree with Phipps that the big difference in such a situation, if it ever really boils down to beating the crap out of each other, won't be any combat power, but the simple fact that Kindred can Embrace at any time.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555373#post1555373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bloodlines may actually be the ending of the Great Leap Outward</b>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think it's both good and bad for it.<br /> <br /> Good because the whole thing is, frankly, stupid. It's not only a poorly thought story, it's a bad story through and through that adds nothing to the game except Chinese orcs.<br /> <br /> Bad because it's a stupid end to this story, and one that doesn't leave a good taste. Partly that's because <i>Bloodlines</i> in general, despite the great story, is ridiculous on having a fledgling do everything the PC does, but overall the whole massacre against the Kuei-Jin is stretching too much, especially when you engage an actual elder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555373#post1555373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Among the Kuei Jin, the numbers wiped out by the Fledgling are not replaceable.</div> </div> </div> </div>With an important caveat, though.<br /> <br /> Just as you can't just make more Kuei Jin whenever you want, you also can't prevent them from appearing.<br /> <br /> Not to say, and I think White Wolf missed a golden opportunity not exploring this, that you can <i>convert people to your cause</i>.<br /> <br /> Even though they won't strictly be the same thing, nothing prevents a Kuei Jin from working for the Camarilla or a Kindred from working for their court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T17:37:38-08:00","id":1555381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555378#post1555378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you ignore <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>' points (and I think they're fair even if not necessarily the original intent of the authors), conflicts of this scale are not just a series of PC fights. PCs get away doing things directly because they're the protagonists of a story, their actions are aggrandized by design, but the bulk of the conflict isn't like that. And I agree with Phipps that the big difference in such a situation, if it ever really boils down to beating the crap out of each other, won't be any combat power, but the simple fact that Kindred can Embrace at any time.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion of the Great Leap Outward is that it mostly makes sense from Doylist reasons rather than Watsonian. The event was created to give Storytellers of Western vampires a reason to buy the new gameline and give a reason for PCs to interact with the Wan Kuei. This versus the Banu Haqim's version. I.e. &quot;The Assamites are now sending diplomats to the Kindred of the West because they have their own problems and want to make peace.&quot; For the Wan Kuei, they decided that players would much rather fight them as monsters and that came with a lot of in-universe and out of universe ugliness.<br /> \u200b<br /> The theory I presented that the Wan Kuei did this to wipe out younger Wan Kuei is not my own but one that I think is canon but I admit I didn't have access to nearly as many books as other people did on the subject (including at my table). I remember this was presented on the forums of the original White Wolf board as fact so I kind of hope someone out there knows for sure if this was canon or just an interpretation.<br /> <br /> Still, I think it works better and actually think the Night of Prophecy take on the subject was better. At the end of the day, the Wan Kuei may not be Cainites but they are VAMPIRES and full of all the political bullshit that implies. I also like the possibility of younger Wan Kuei finding they have more in common with Anarchs than they do their Elders.<br /> <br /> (The Dance of the Thrashing Dragon mod on Bloodlines is also good for presenting this)\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think it's both good and bad for it.<br /> <br /> Good because the whole thing is, frankly, stupid. It's not only a poorly thought story, it's a bad story through and through that adds nothing to the game except Chinese orcs.<br /> <br /> Bad because it's a stupid end to this story, and one that doesn't leave a good taste. Partly that's because <i>Bloodlines</i> in general, despite the great story, is ridiculous on having a fledgling do everything the PC does, but overall the whole massacre against the Kuei-Jin is stretching too much, especially when you engage an actual elder. </div> </div> </div>I think I give it a pass due to the fact that it has issues but at least it's an ending. I feel like with so many dangling plot threads leftover from the end of the line that it at least provides answers. Maybe not the most satisfying answers but at least answers.<br /> <br /> I also tend to embrace the comic book nature of V:TM versus trying to make it follow absolutely consistent rules. Some Kindred are just built different and are able to rapidly gain power to match much older entities.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With an important caveat, though.<br /> <br /> Just as you can't just make more Kuei Jin whenever you want, you also can't prevent them from appearing.<br /> <br /> Not to say, and I think White Wolf missed a golden opportunity not exploring this, that you can <i>convert people to your cause</i>.<br /> <br /> Even though they won't strictly be the same thing, nothing prevents a Kuei Jin from working for the Camarilla or a Kindred from working for their court. </div> </div> </div>Very true.<br /> <br /> Especially since the Kuei Jin are a group that COULD ally with way more supernaturals than most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T19:40:59-08:00","id":1555382,"title":"","content":"I understand the Great Leap Outward from a Doylist perspective, but don't <i>agree</i> with it. It's still a bad story, not just because of all the problematic stuff (and holy shit, they're problematic), but simply because presenting the new splat through a protracted war devoid of any dept is kinda dumb. You literally want people to engage those characters, and you'll do that by having them want to kill each other?<br /> <br /> But I don't think this theory of it boiling down to an attempt at wiping out their young was ever canonical, at least not as a fact. It may have been raised once or twice as a theory, but nothing deeper AFAIK. And I don't think it would be the best, either, because it creates an obvious, big, problem: now all those young are away from your main propaganda machine and exposed to new ideas and easy access to freedom. The risk of desertion and possibly rebellion is too big and too obvious. The only reason it didn't happened and in numbers was that WW didn't thought about it. It wasn't really that important for them.<br /> <br /> On the Fledgling and their antics, including against the Kuei-Jin, I mostly agree, I was just saying it has a downside. I'm on the fence if it will be truth in my games, but overall I'm good with <i>Bloodlines</i> being canon with everything that entails. I just wonder what the Fledgling would be doing now, IF they survived.<br /> <br /> My personal opinion, and including the fact that I think both Kindred and Hungry Dead should have a greater presence in every continent, is that total war between the splats is unlikely and uninteresting. They would most probably keep tabs on each other and reach some kind of mutual understanding, if only for the same reason they each do so internally: they need the same resources and both risk depleting it if they go too far. Fighting is rarely to anyone's benefit. Sure, sometimes it happens, but not a global war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T20:00:01-08:00","id":1555384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555381#post1555381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very true.<br /> <br /> Especially since the Kuei Jin are a group that COULD ally with way more supernaturals than most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to the demands of some Dharmas and any spirits that any particular Gui Ren might be allied with, they might be only slightly better at this than the Garou. Resplendent Cranes, Devil Tigers, and a lot of Thrashing Dragons probably represent diplomatic liabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T22:07:30-08:00","id":1555390,"title":"","content":"This was one of the more stupid metaplot elements of Revised. I ignore it completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T00:17:01-08:00","id":1555392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton#post1555369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about the whole situation and how plausible that sounded.<br /> Similarly I have heard arguments for either side, Kuei Jin and Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; is a very complex thing<br /> Starting with the basics, lets unpack it, shall we?<br /> The Middle Kingdom is geographically and spiritually is only defined as\u2026 well not defined at all!<br /> Considering how important the term is it is very surprising\u2026<br /> Officially the Middle Kingdom is the umbrella term for China, Japan, India, Bangladesh, Korea, Laos, Mongolia, the Philippines, Singapore, Taiwan, Thailand, Tibet and Vietnam<br /> In the 1000 Hell Book, a very little line about the Yama Kings. Actually it is their &quot;fault&quot; there are bo &quot;wstern Kuei-jin&quot;. When they &quot;built&quot; Yomi, expanding their domain by tearing part out the Yin and Yang worlds (Umbra/Dark Umbra) and the Middle Kingdom (Material) and conducting rituals to modify thir original role as purifiers and redeemers, necessary jailors who obeyed the August Personage of Jade. (As such, they had their own pocket dimensions where they enacted their necessary, if unpleasant, duties.) so the sinners would still end up in their little Hells, they locked themselves out from the western hemispehre, but at the time they saw only &quot;barbarians&quot; there (I doubt in their eyes that changed) and not really considered that a loss. The &quot;role&quot; of Yomi was somewhat filled by Malfeas and the Maeljins in the West (the book even mentions, they have some &quot;diplomatic&quot; relationship between Yomi and Malfeas, slave caravans, gifts coming back and forth and lots of lots of smiles, and while they would gleefully tear each other apart, Malfeas is too chaotic to muster a real invasion force to attack Yomi, where in their home turf, the Yama Kings are literally Gods with armies of Demonic servants and the Yama Kings rearlly capable of working together more than 5 minutes without ploting to stab the each others in the back and annex the falle Yama King's relam to organize an attack, and even if one side would attack, the cost would be too high and overall, the whole war is pointless, the Demon Emperor and the Sixth age is coming)<br /> So the Yama Kings &quot;tied&quot; Yomi to the Middle Kingdom<br /> But here is the catch<br /> The borders of the Middle Kingdom are not set in stone, they actually move<br /> For example Mongolia was/is part of the Middle Kingdom and before his demise the Yama King Dokhor-Khan, ruler of the Hell of Spiked Chains, claimed the souls of mortals that had died in the steppes<br /> Russia... is huge<br /> Half of Russia basically, the once Mongol territories and Siberia are in North Asia - it IS North Asia!<br /> It was part of the lands of the Black Tortoise Court and the &quot;borders&quot; always moved<br /> (To the point they may even clasehd Baba Yaga who was old enough to see maybe the fall of the Wan Xian and her magic was tied to her Land - not unlike Koldunism, she was a shaman and had her own dealings with both the Yin and Yang words\u2026 different story and if I would go deeper in this we would be here all day and night)<br /> So where the Kuei-jin go, goes Yomi and the Whole area of spiritual influence of the Middle Kingdom\u2026<br /> K\u00e0nbuji\u00e0n at first glance complicate this; they are Kuei-jin that have taken the Second Breath outside the Middle Kingdom and somehow managed to transcend their chih-mei phase out of sheer force of will.<br /> But actually you don't have to be phisically present in the middle kingdom to rise as a Kuei-Jin the only criteria to become one, so to speak is for your soul is to land in Yomi, then claw your way out of Yomi<br /> The Yama Kings have a very organized &quot;System&quot; who can claim what; Emma-o presiding over the souls of the despised and dishonorable, Ravana presiding over the souls of the violent, Hine-Nui-Te-Po, presiding over the souls of those who committed suicide, Dokhor-Khan, claimed the souls of mortals that had died in the steppes, etc. You just have to have some spiritual tie to the Middle Kingdom, ancestor maybe or something like that<br /> Now here comes the magician's trick!<br /> This spiritual influence and the rach of Yomi explands<br /> The &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; is actually not a new thing; before and during the Victorian Age, there had been sightings of Wan Kuei in places like Istanbul and St. Petersburg.<br /> Expatriates have reached Chinatowns all over the world, though the concentration is highest in the United States. Cities that have a Kuei-jin population are Boston, New York City and London (any attempts of the Kuei-jin to colonize Chicago, however, have failed thanks to Menele..) and Vancouver is a traditional stronghold of House Bishamon among the Clans of the Sun<br /> And this is an important part<br /> The &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; at first glance is basically offensive of the Kuei-jin against domains of western vampires outside the Middle Kingdom, a colonization from the Middle Kingdom's part but actually\u2026?<br /> The &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; is the pet project of the Quincunx &quot;alliance&quot; - the ruling body of the Kuei-Jin Courts of China - and mainly the Blood Court of Beijing.<br /> Contrary of popular belief the Quincunx don't rule the Kuei-Jin nor the Middle Kingdom<br /> The Previously mentioned House Bishamon and the Clans of the Sun are the Kuei-jin of Japan and quite resistant of the Quincunx influence, the Green Court is the ruling body of the Kuei-Jin of Korea (a sort of neutral ground between the Quincunx and the Japanese Uji) tried to stay out (but watch it with great interest and scooped up a few Nagaraja refugees) but sends its wu to undermine every effort of establishing permanent Courts outside the Middle Kingdom, fearing what it will bode for them...<br /> Australia was not targeted by the Quincunx, but by luminaries of House Genji - the historical opposition of House Bishamon (it is an intersting situation there, see the book Shadow War for details, worth it)<br /> The Golden Courts (conglomeration of loosely allied domains under the control of Kuei-jin matriarchsof Southeast Asia) have no involvement in the Great Leap Outward like how the Infinite Thunder Courts (the area of India and into Bangladesh) similarly not really participate<br /> Strangely enough, a whole Dharma, the Resplendant Cranes regardless of their regional affiliation, after seeing the success of the New Promise Mandarinate, have begun to discuss what regions of the world should next be targeted. Some suggest Peru and others started eyeing Russia after Baba Yaga checked out<br /> <br /> The main effect of the &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; is the fact the Kuei-jin carry the reach of the Yomi World with them.<br /> This allows the Yama Kings to access resources that they do not have within their traditional domains.<br /> The Yama King that most profits from the Great Leap Outward is Mikaboshi, who has several Broken Mirrors (places where the boundaries between the Material World and Yomi Wan have been loosened by massive amounts of mortal suffering, Tainted Chi and desolate spirits) within San Francisco<br /> <br /> SO<br /> The &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; is a very compklicated social, spiritual and military situation with several players on several levels and sides with potential long term consequences<br /> Historically the Kuei-jin and the Middle Kingdom is not that bad at &quot;colonizing&quot; and spreading their influence - smiliarly the Cainites are quite good in exporting their own kind and rule, but unlike the Cainites who may or may not attract the ire of Spirits, ghosts, shapeshifters the Kuei-jin literally carry the Hells with them who have a very Strong interest to see this little pet project succeed and even if they are not Akumas any Yama King potentially could interfere to tip the favor of any conflict between the two sides (but possibly not without consequences either; Rangda presiding over the diseased, her best interest to spread disease; in the past century has filled her with a dark glee as first Japanese germ warfare in China and now Southeast Asia's HIV epidemic cause er empire to grow in leaps and bounds. Her servants work to hasten the spread of sickness however they can, be it through the prevention of health education, the encouragement of unregulated prostitution, or cutting-edge research in the fields of nuclear and biochemical warfare\u2026 and this may or may not attracts the attention and their own little cold war with the Maeljin Lady Yul, the Mistress of Toxins)<br /> <br /> The deck is a bit stacked you see; the Cainites are not that well versed of the Yin and Yang World and Hells like the Kuei-jin<br /> On the other hand the Kuei-jin are unfamilar with the local spirits and ghosts and kinda used to the cold but cordial realtionship with the Beast Courts and not really would understand why the local shifters are so violently barbaric... and the last thing they want to be associated with Yomi<br /> <br /> If we - sorry for the better Word - domb it down only to a Wu vs. Coterie situation, then it is depends on the situation and Wu and Coterie, it is a 50-50% who would win, but I would say a Kuei-jin Wu even without a Nushi probably would fold a cainite coterie most of the time simply because of the rigid traning (In the old nights, this training process might last a full 24 years, two cycles of the zodiac, but in the fifth age it shortened down to around 5 years);they have to survive before going thrugh the Fire and Water Test, their rite of passage of sort and untill then the Court and teachers edducate and train them; the Cainites lack this even if the Sire focuses on the teaching, a Kuei-jin spends her first years with their future wu members trying not to die and fail and I think this gives them an edge in a situatio with a coterie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T05:32:53-08:00","id":1555400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555392#post1555392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; is a very complex thing</div> </div> </div> </div>I really would like it if you used more spaces between paragraphs. You're a good writer, but those blocks are hard to read and I'm with a headache for real now.<br /> <br /> But I would like to know how much of this is explicitly stated on the books as fact, by whom, and how much is conjecture or legend in the books.<br /> <br /> Do the Wan-Kuei know about the Yomi's influence? Which of them do?<br /> <br /> And is there any justification for their arrival to be hostile?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T05:43:47-08:00","id":1555401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555392#post1555392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; is a very complex thing<br /> Starting with the basics, lets unpack it, shall we?</div> </div> </div> </div>A very complex and interesting spiritual dissertation but I don't think it's the kind of thing that actually would have any real effects to the &quot;boots on the ground.&quot; Because at the end of the day, the conflict of the Great Leap Outward as you're presenting it would be handled fine by...<br /> <br /> &quot;Buying a plane ticket, buying a house&quot;<br /> <br /> Versus waging a complicated and costly war against the endless hordes of Potence and Celerity wielding Brujah there.<br /> <br /> You've certainly established a lot of reasons for the Lords of Hell to want to spread the Kuei Jin (their natural enemies) but not really given a reason why they want to pick a fight with the Cainites.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that the Underworld of the West in WOD is an absolute mess following the destruction of Stygia, the death of one of the Neverborn (kudos to Charon for that one, I'll give him that since we've established those guys as literal Princes of Hell and the gods of the Nephandus), and the various Maelstroms that would possibly give them pause.<br /> <br /> Certainly, Malpheas is a big deal but....very little related to fighting Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Which is a long and short way of saying, &quot;I can certainly see this argument presented but at the end of the day I am inclined to go with the Great Leap Outward's motives and activities is petty not grandiose.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind you, I also note about vampires vs. werewolves: &quot;werewolves will always win in a fair fight against anything but a Methuselah as they fight in packs but when have vampires ever fought fair?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-12-2025, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T06:40:11-08:00","id":1555403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555400#post1555400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really would like it if you used more spaces between paragraphs. You're a good writer, but those blocks are hard to read and I'm with a headache for real now.<br /> <br /> But I would like to know how much of this is explicitly stated on the books as fact, by whom, and how much is conjecture or legend in the books.<br /> <br /> Do the Wan-Kuei know about the Yomi's influence? Which of them do?<br /> <br /> And is there any justification for their arrival to be hostile?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will try, I promise <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> San Francisco by Night write about the Broken Mirrors a bit more detailed the the 1000 Hells (this also touches the Yomi influence)<br /> Along with them and Shadow War (this one even mentions one of the Jade Court' bodhisattvas voicing criticism against the campaign and concern - prophecy actually, that the Great Leap Outward would only weaken the Blood Court in the long run, although no one listened to him) and the Dharma Books they touch the subject <br /> <br /> All an all, <i>some</i> Kuei-jin have made the connection about the spreading Yomi-influence - or the reson behind it eg. the &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; - but generally they remained silent in fear of voicing their suspicions too loud<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T08:40:57-08:00","id":1555410,"title":"","content":"Nice discussion!<br /> <br /> though I think the last line was missed. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's keep it relatively simple and street level. </div> </div> </div>you guys are going in too deep. I am aware it is a complicated question and one could go quite deep into it. Thus I just want to deal with a simple, limited scenario. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555373#post1555373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>1. What is the actual goal of the Great Leap Outward?</b><br /> <b>2. The logistics of the Great Leap Outward favor the Western Kindred</b><br /> <b>3. The two major powers don't actually care</b><br /> <b>4. Bloodlines may actually be the ending of the Great Leap Outward</b></div> </div> </div> </div>1. that's just silly. they already kill most freshly risen hungry corpses. If they are getting too numerous - just make 'passing' standards stricter. <br /> 2. I do agree and already mentioned it. <br /> 3. not relevant. we are talking a street level confrontation. <br /> 4. maybe, but again - not relevant in this specific case. Not to mention, technically speaking Miaos death is entirely dependent how she was killed. If body was left relatively intact - she can come back from that. Similar with other Kuei jin in the temple. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that the whole exercise is skewed and oversimplified. </div> </div> </div>yeap. exactly the point. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just as you can't just make more Kuei Jin whenever you want, you also can't prevent them from appearing. </div> </div> </div>yeah, I do not remember exact book but Kuei Jin now appear everywhere. with asia having enough humans and no competing vampires so they could develop and organize. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First things first, neither build is really likely. Starting characters by the rules are PCs, they're young, but above average, not representatives of what an average character of that age will be like. Or any age, because on top of that characters within the story are unlikely to follow any &quot;combo&quot;, as they don't develop their stats to fill a PC role, they just live their lives. So characters on each side will vary greatly and very few, even if selected as warriors, will be anything like a combat-oriented PC. </div> </div> </div>I know. But there are so many varieties of possible combinations that I have chosen to select a likely and simplified teams. Also not giving them quite a few tools available to starting PCs - like magical items. But I do not think lvl2 disciplines is overkill for trained combatant. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Due to the demands of some Dharmas and any spirits that any particular Gui Ren might be allied with, they might be only slightly better at this than the Garou. Resplendent Cranes, Devil Tigers, and a lot of Thrashing Dragons probably represent diplomatic liabilities. </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt is entirely possible. But also entirely depends which faction they are approaching. I do not think redcaps would be grossed out by Thrashing dragons.<br /> The garou are problem on street level, because most of them would think Kuei jin weird fomori or something. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the 1000 Hell Book, a very little line about the Yama Kings. Actually it is their &quot;fault&quot; there are bo &quot;wstern Kuei-jin&quot;. </div> </div> </div>got retconned as far as I remember in 20th edition. One of the book mentions them. Apparently now they appear all around the world, but generally stay as mindless cannibal corpses without the proper methods to bring their minds back. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But here is the catch<br /> The borders of the Middle Kingdom are not set in stone, they actually move </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> this one is actually easy enough. WoD is not IRL. reality is malleable and asian 'reality bubble' has a bit different rules concerning magical side. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Historically the Kuei-jin and the Middle Kingdom is not that bad at &quot;colonizing&quot; and spreading their influence - smiliarly the Cainites are quite good in exporting their own kind and rule, but unlike the Cainites who may or may not attract the ire of Spirits, ghosts, shapeshifters the Kuei-jin literally carry the Hells with them who have a very Strong interest to see this little pet project succeed and even if they are not Akumas any Yama King potentially could interfere to tip the favor of any conflict </div> </div> </div>That is a good point. But on the other hand, Kuei JIn have more interest in preserving nature/natural order being more attuned to spirit worlds. So they have some common ground with others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-12T09:51:41-08:00","id":1555414,"title":"","content":"One other front to expand the ranges where Hungry Dead show up involves Mikaboshi, who broke into the CyberRealm in Revised. As a master of geomancy (it's how he broke into hell as a ruler in the first place), he might be capable of expanding his rule from there as a vantage point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T15:26:13-08:00","id":1555437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555410#post1555410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">though I think the last line was missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't.<br /> <br /> Street level doesn't answer your question in any meaningful way, and the fact that it is complex <u><b>is</b></u> the simple answer, and the rest are examples.<br /> <br /> Also, this is a forum. People will answer however they feel like. Asking people to not elaborate kind of misses the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555410#post1555410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus I just want to deal with a simple, limited scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that your scenario is inadequate to address the point.<br /> <br /> Even if you had actually relevant stats for them, comparing single individuals in a straight fight may be fun, but doesn't really say anything about the conflict because it's not how the conflict unfolds in any meaningful way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555410#post1555410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. that's just silly. they already kill most freshly risen hungry corpses. If they are getting too numerous - just make 'passing' standards stricter.<br /> 2. I do agree and already mentioned it.<br /> 3. not relevant. we are talking a street level confrontation.<br /> 4. maybe, but again - not relevant in this specific case. Not to mention, technically speaking Miaos death is entirely dependent how she was killed. If body was left relatively intact - she can come back from that. Similar with other Kuei jin in the temple.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The whole thing is silly, already. That said, though, they can't simply change the rules of their society without having a whole upheaval, that's simply not how things work. Their current standard is already quite objective, changing it will be seen by their current underlings as straight murder and things won't be good from there;<br /> 2. No, you didn't. His point is that the <i>logistics</i> favor the Kindred, not the power set. You focused on the differences in builds and power set, and everyone else basically tried to tell you that this isn't the point;<br /> 3. Even in a street level confrontation, the investment of the powers-that-be greatly helps define the assets and options the people in the streets have access to. So even at this level they do matter;<br /> 4. How's the direct presence of an active Elder not relevant in this case? She literally <i>can</i> put her personal resources and even herself in the line from time to time. Or, rather, could when alive.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555410#post1555410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeap. exactly the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some times simplified scenarios don't answer our question because we established a question that requires something else.<br /> <br /> This is one such case.<br /> <br /> You actually didn't stipulate your question, which is one of the main reasons for the discussion to wander so much. But the point everyone made was that the one-on-one exercise seems irrelevant to the Great Leap Outward. Like, completely irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Maybe you can posit an actual question that makes this comparison relevant. But just saying it is about the Great Leap Outward, you'll only get the answer that it is unimportant.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555410#post1555410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know. But there are so many varieties of possible combinations that I have chosen to select a likely and simplified teams. Also not giving them quite a few tools available to starting PCs - like magical items. But I do not think lvl2 disciplines is overkill for trained combatant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your builds aren't likely, for a few reasons I'll try to unpack here:<br /> <br /> There being so many varieties of possible combinations <b><u>is the point</u></b>. Any specific build is only relevant if it is likely. Since we're not comparing PC builds, but what someone will find in the actual fiction, how the setting proposes that regular NPCs organically develop matters, and this isn't someone with 6 dice at everything combat. Much less of a particular clan or whatever, even if you can expect more Brujah than normal in this particular city.<br /> <br /> Supernatural powers are hard to come by and to increase, most characters are expected to have incredibly slow advancement rates and begin &quot;play&quot; so to speak with less stats than a starting PC, because <b>PCs are special in every way</b>, remember that. So while your numbers are conservative for PCs, they're actually way over the top for the regular person in the street, specially the 6 total dots in Disciplines and the impressive WP.<br /> <br /> Most Neonates are still more informed by their living days than whatever they got as vampires, and vampires rarely Embraced looking only towards their most immediate needs, because wars end, but the Right to Embrace doesn't come often. So most won't be Embracing pure muscle, and soldiers and other professional combatants not only aren't all that desired, they also aren't all that common. Even gang members and other criminals, while <i>trained</i> in combat, are unlikely to have builds <i>completely devoted</i> to combat. They're people with an actual civilian life to live. So the very idea of professional combatants facing each other is actually unlikely.<br /> <br /> Even their equipment is outlandish as a <i>likely</i> or <i>standard</i> thing. To begin with California has some of the most restrictive gun laws in the US and a population less interested in owning guns. It is still a lot by the standards of most other countries, but way below the US average. So what? That means your average Joe, including your average vampire, isn't actually likely to have a gun to begin with. Even though a vampire has an easier time procuring a gun and won't bother with laws, the point is that most are unlikely to want one or know how to use it. Add to that supernatural powers and resistance make most vampires more prone to go melee if they have to fight at all (and to flee instead of fight an equal if that's an option). On top of that, <i>Desert Eagles</i> and <i>Bowie Knives</i> are far from common weapons. They're both expensive, hard to acquire and draw a lot of attention. And I mean expensive, both are several times the price you'll pay for a simpler item.<br /> <br /> Ghouls are there to make up for those problems. Ghouling a security guard or police officer, or a gang member, is the simplest way of getting someone with the actual training and a firearm without wasting a too valuable Embrace and all the trouble a Fledgling brings just so you have a muscle to send.<br /> <br /> A real average build is more in line with this: 2-4 Discipline dots randomly spread through in-clans. Most Attributes at 2, with at most two at 3, also random. Random Abilities, most with 1 dot, a few with 2 dots that are areas they work regularly or are professionals at, one or two at 3 <b>IF</b> this is an established professional at the trade. WP 1-4. <i>Maybe</i> a pocketknife or switchblade if they expect trouble, sometimes a Glock 19 or similar if they're a gun user. No specific clan. If you want a likely trained combatant, it's 3 dots spread among in-clans with none at 3, 4 dice for most combat rolls, 5 or 6 at some only if they're especially good or a veteran, WP 3 because of high <b>Courage</b>, and a switchblade. Anything above is possible, but not average or likely in any meaningful way.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555410#post1555410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIt is entirely possible. But also entirely depends which faction they are approaching. I do not think redcaps would be grossed out by Thrashing dragons.<br /> The garou are problem on street level, because most of them would think Kuei jin weird fomori or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings are possibly the least likely splat to get involved, just because knowing about them or interacting with them is hard unless <i>they</i> go after you.<br /> <br /> And they're also the least predictable splat, because you'll either bring very few of them, or you'll bring their attention <i>en masse</i> and then you'll have a whole court of invisible fae taking sides and involving everyone in their shenanigans.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555410#post1555410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">got retconned as far as I remember in 20th edition. One of the book mentions them. Apparently now they appear all around the world, but generally stay as mindless cannibal corpses without the proper methods to bring their minds back.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole debacle did, IIRC. If we're talking seriously the Great Leap Outward, we're not talking 20th &quot;lore&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T15:40:48-08:00","id":1555438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555381#post1555381\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555381#post1555381\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555381#post1555381\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555369-great-leap-outwards-quesiton?p=1555381#post1555381 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My post above was caught up in approval until now. It's now up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}